“Same fabric” means the compute tile and the PCT don’t each have their own incompatible network. They share one common interconnect and protocol that spans both dies. A block on the PCT talks to a block on the compute tile the same way it would talk to a neighbor on its own die.
IP (intellectual property block)
In chip design, an IP is a reusable functional block: a USB controller, a PCIe controller, a memory controller, a media engine, an NPU. Each is designed once and dropped into different chips.
Why a shared fabric lets you “move IPs between dies”
Every block talks to the rest of the system through the fabric’s interface. If that interface is identical on both dies, a block doesn’t care which die it sits on. The designers can decide where each IP lives without redesigning how it connects.

